<% html_title 'Performance', 'Periodic Time' %>
<% content_for :header_tags do %>
  <%= stylesheet_link_tag 'performance', plugin: 'redmine_ticket_journey' %>
  <%= javascript_include_tag 'performance_owner_picker', plugin: 'redmine_ticket_journey', defer: true %>
  <%= javascript_include_tag 'performance_navigation', plugin: 'redmine_ticket_journey', defer: true %>
  <%= javascript_include_tag 'performance_leaderboard', plugin: 'redmine_ticket_journey', defer: true %>
<% end %>
<div class="performance-page periodic-page periodic-time-page">
  <%= render 'header', page_title: 'Periodic Performance — Time' %>
  <p class="periodic-provisional"><strong>Provisional Time rules — confirmation pending.</strong> Ticket costs include visible direct hours from all contributors through RED. Personal hours follow the logged user (time-entry user_id) and use RSD–RED work dates. <a href="#periodic-time-rules">Read the time windows and calculation rules</a>.</p>
  <p class="performance-context">Same Periodic expectation package, visible project hierarchy and tracker scope · Recorded completion with current-status checks · Current owners, estimates, weights, priority and calendar settings</p>
  <% if @periodic_time_report %>
    <% report = @periodic_time_report %>
    <p><strong><%= @owner_label %></strong> · Workdays per owner: <%= @calendar.days(@period_start, @period_end) %><% if @selected_owners.any? { |owner| !owner.active? } %> · Includes inactive owners from saved selections.<% end %></p>
    <% unless report[:available] %><p class="periodic-provisional">Time-view permission is incomplete in the selected project hierarchy. Scoped total/daily hours and Other Work comparisons are unavailable; known visible hours and contributor coverage remain disclosed. Unavailable data is not zero.</p><% end %>
    <section class="performance-section periodic-summary">
      <h3>Plan / Actual Time Results<%= ' — Team' if @selected_owners.size > 1 %></h3>
      <details><summary>Show plan, actual and deviations</summary><%= render 'periodic_time_table', report: report, ids: @selected_owner_ids %></details>
      <% if @selected_owners.size > 1 %><details><summary>Show owner comparisons and individual deviations</summary>
        <% TicketJourneyPeriodicTime::METRICS.each do |key, (label, unit, _direction)| %>
          <details><summary><%= label %> (<%= unit %>)</summary>
            <div class="autoscroll"><table class="list"><thead><tr><th>Owner</th><th>Plan</th><th>Actual</th><th>Performance Deviation</th><th>Deviation %</th></tr></thead><tbody>
              <% (@periodic_time_owners + [{ owner: nil, report: report }]).each do |item| %><% entry = item[:report][:metrics][key]; ids = item[:owner] ? [item[:owner].id.to_s] : @selected_owner_ids %>
                <tr class="<%= 'periodic-total-row' unless item[:owner] %>"><th><%= item[:owner]&.name || 'Team aggregate' %></th><td><%= periodic_time_number(entry[:plan], key) %></td><td><%= periodic_time_link(periodic_time_number(entry[:actual], key), key, ids) %></td><td class="<%= periodic_time_class(key, entry) %>"><%= periodic_time_deviation(key, entry) %></td><td><%= entry[:deviation].nil? || entry[:deviation][:percent].nil? ? 'N/A' : "#{performance_number(entry[:deviation][:percent])}%" %></td></tr>
              <% end %>
            </tbody></table></div>
          </details>
        <% end %>
      </details><% end %>
    </section>

    <section class="performance-section"><h3>Time Performance</h3>
      <div class="periodic-time-kpis"><% TicketJourneyPeriodicTime::METRICS.each do |key, (label, unit, _direction)| %><% entry = report[:metrics][key] %>
        <article class="performance-metric periodic-time-kpi"><h4><%= label %></h4><strong><%= periodic_time_link(periodic_time_number(entry[:actual], key), key) %> <small><%= unit %></small></strong>
          <p>Plan / Target: <b><%= periodic_time_number(entry[:plan], key) %></b> <%= unit %></p>
          <p class="<%= periodic_time_class(key, entry) %>"><b><%= periodic_time_deviation(key, entry) %></b><% if entry[:deviation] && entry[:deviation][:percent] %> · <%= performance_number(entry[:deviation][:percent]) %>%<% end %></p>
          <small><%= periodic_time_link("#{entry[:rows].size} ticket-owner contributions", key) %></small>
          <% if key == 'other_hours' %><p>Extra Work: <%= periodic_time_number(entry[:extra_hours], key) %> h · Unplanned: <%= periodic_time_number(entry[:unplanned_hours], key) %> h</p><% end %>
        </article>
      <% end %></div>
      <p class="performance-weight-note">DTC targets and owner-share % are configured under Administration → Plugins → PMO Dashboard → Configure. Blank targets remain N/A. Ticket cost overrun within the configured <%= performance_number(@estimate_allowance) %>% allowance is amber; exceeding it is red. Other negative deviations are red. Low visible hours alone do not establish efficiency or completed work.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="periodic-grid">
      <section class="performance-section"><h3>Ticket Cost — Plan vs Actual</h3>
        <% cost = report[:metrics]['ticket_cost']; maximum = [[cost[:plan], cost[:actual]].compact.max.to_f, 1].max %>
        <% [:plan, :actual].each do |kind| %><div class="periodic-bar-row"><span><%= kind == :plan ? 'PM Estimate' : 'Visible Direct Hours through RED' %></span><div class="periodic-bar-track"><%= periodic_time_link(content_tag(:span, '', class: 'periodic-bar-fill', style: "width:#{cost[kind].to_f * 100 / maximum}%;"), 'ticket_cost', @selected_owner_ids, 'aria-label': "#{kind}: #{periodic_time_number(cost[kind], 'ticket_cost')} hours") %></div><b><%= periodic_time_number(cost[kind], 'ticket_cost') %> h</b></div><% end %>
        <p>All Done Tickets, including Other Done. Both bars use the same positive-estimate/time-available tickets. Full visible direct cost through RED includes earlier work and excludes child rollups.</p>
        <p><%= periodic_time_link("Excluded done tickets: #{report[:sets]['cost_excluded'].size}", 'cost_excluded') %> · Full done-population visible cost: <%= periodic_time_number(report[:all_done_visible_cost], 'ticket_cost') %> h</p>
      </section>
      <section class="performance-section"><h3>Personal Hours — Reconciliation</h3>
        <p>Known visible hours: <strong><%= periodic_time_number(report[:valid_visible_hours], 'total_hours') %> h</strong>. All four categories below use logged users and work dates in the selected period.</p>
        <table class="list"><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Hours</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <% [['expected_done', 'Completed expected work', 'expected_done_all'], ['expected_unfinished', 'Unfinished expected work', 'expected_unfinished'], ['other', 'Other tickets (including cross-owner work)', 'other_hours'], ['unclassified', 'Ticket Owner unavailable', 'unclassified']].each do |key, label, metric| %><tr><th><%= label %></th><td><%= periodic_time_link(periodic_time_number(report[:breakdown][key], 'total_hours'), metric) %></td></tr><% end %>
        </tbody></table>
        <p>Expected Done comparable card: <%= periodic_time_number(report[:metrics]['expected_done_hours'][:actual], 'total_hours') %> h. All Expected Done hours: <%= periodic_time_number(report[:expected_done_raw_hours], 'total_hours') %> h. Missing estimates/time can explain the difference.</p>
        <p><%= periodic_time_link("Expected Done comparison exclusions: #{report[:sets]['expected_done_excluded'].size}", 'expected_done_excluded') %></p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="performance-section"><h3>Expected Work Completion</h3>
      <% completion = @periodic_time_completion; percent = performance_percent(completion['completed'][:count], completion['expected'][:count]) %>
      <div class="periodic-completion"><div class="performance-donut" role="img" aria-label="Expected work completion: <%= percent.nil? ? 'N/A' : "#{performance_number(percent)}%" %>" style="background:conic-gradient(#00865e 0% <%= percent || 0 %>%, #e7edf3 <%= percent || 0 %>% 100%)"><div><strong><%= percent.nil? ? 'N/A' : "#{performance_number(percent)}%" %></strong><span><%= completion['completed'][:count] %> / <%= completion['expected'][:count] %></span></div></div>
        <div><% %w[expected completed other debt].each do |key| %><p><%= TicketJourneyPeriodicTickets::LABELS[key] %>: <%= periodic_ticket_link(completion[key][:count], key) %> tickets · <%= performance_number(completion[key][:weight]) %> CW</p><% end %></div>
      </div>
      <p>Other Work is favorable Extra Work only for an owner with a nonempty, fully delivered expectation package and zero debt at RED. Team results keep favorable and unplanned hours separate.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="periodic-grid">
      <%= render 'periodic_time_trend', chart_key: 'dtc', title: 'Days to Close — Completion Cohorts', series: periodic_time_trend_series(%w[dtc priority_dtc]), description: 'Calendar days from creation to latest qualifying completion. Each point uses the final RED done population completed in that interval; targets are current global settings.' %>
      <%= render 'periodic_time_trend', chart_key: 'cost', title: 'Ticket Cost — Completion Cohorts', series: periodic_time_trend_series(['ticket_cost']), description: 'PM estimate versus full visible direct ticket hours through RED for each completion cohort, including work before RSD. These are delivered-ticket costs, not hours logged only during the cohort.' %>
      <%= render 'periodic_time_trend', chart_key: 'total', title: 'Owner Logged Hours — Work-Date Intervals', series: periodic_time_trend_series(['total_hours']), description: 'Actual uses visible valid entries booked to the selected users in each interval. Plan is owner-workdays × configured daily hours, summed across owners.' %>
      <%= render 'periodic_time_trend', chart_key: 'daily', title: 'Average Logged Hours per Owner-Workday', series: periodic_time_trend_series(['daily_hours']), description: 'Sum logged hours divided by sum owner-workdays. Partial weeks use their actual configured working days; zero-workday points are unavailable.' %>
      <%= render 'periodic_time_trend', chart_key: 'efficiency', title: 'Delivered Expected Complexity Weight / Owner Hour', series: periodic_time_trend_series(['efficiency']), description: 'Actual uses delivered expected weight in the completion interval divided by owner work-date hours on the paired full expectation portfolio, including unfinished work. Plan is the full portfolio weight / configured expected effort, a rate reference rather than a weekly allocation.' %>
      <%= render 'periodic_time_breakdown' %>
    </div>
    <% if @selected_owners.size > 1 %>
      <% %w[dtc priority_dtc ticket_cost expected_done_hours total_hours daily_hours efficiency].each do |key| %>
        <% series = @selected_owners.flat_map do |owner|
          kinds = key == 'expected_done_hours' ? [:actual] : [:actual, :plan]
          kinds.map do |kind|
            { key: key, kind: kind, metric: key, label: "#{owner.name} — #{kind.to_s.titleize}", owner_name: owner.name, owner_id: owner.id.to_s, ids: [owner.id.to_s], color: performance_owner_color(owner.id), dashed: kind == :plan,
              points: @periodic_time_trends.map { |point| { date: point[:date], start: point[:start], value: point[:owners].find { |entry| entry[:owner].id == owner.id }[:report][:metrics][key][kind] } } }
          end
        end %>
        <%= render 'periodic_time_trend', chart_key: "owners-#{key}", title: "#{TicketJourneyPeriodicTime::METRICS[key].first} — Individual Owners", series: series, description: 'Individual actual values use the same contributor definitions and date windows as the team charts. Targets and per-owner deviations are available in the top comparison tables.' %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
    <section class="performance-section"><h3>Coverage and Settings</h3>
      <% %w[cost_excluded expected_done_excluded efficiency_excluded dtc_excluded unclassified].each do |key| %><p><%= periodic_time_link("#{TicketJourneyPeriodicTime::LABELS[key]}: #{report[:sets][key].size}", key) %></p><% end %>
      <p>Unavailable/invalid personal-time contributions: <%= report[:invalid_rows] %>. Invalid, negative and nonfinite time is excluded from comparisons, not presented as zero. Owner daily-hour fallbacks: <%= @time_hours_fallback.size %> owner(s).</p>
      <p>Efficiency uses <%= report[:metrics]['efficiency'][:rows].size %> paired ticket-owner contributions: delivered <%= performance_number(report[:metrics]['efficiency'][:delivered_weight]) %> CW / <%= performance_number(report[:metrics]['efficiency'][:actual_effort]) %> owner h. Planned <%= performance_number(report[:metrics]['efficiency'][:expected_weight]) %> CW / <%= performance_number(report[:metrics]['efficiency'][:planned_effort]) %> expected h.</p>
      <p>Totals cover visible issues in the selected project hierarchy, included trackers and current status scope. Time without a ticket, on excluded trackers/statuses, or outside this hierarchy is outside these totals. The capacity plan still represents configured owner availability; partial issue/private-entry visibility may limit logged-hour comparisons.</p>
    </section>
  <% else %><p class="nodata">Select Ticket Owner(s), set the period, and click Apply. Initial navigation does not scan issues or time entries. Configure DTC targets and owner-share % before interpreting target comparisons.</p><% end %>
  <%= render 'periodic_time_rules' %>
</div>
